From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:59:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 102/107] clk: meson: t7: keep the HDMI PLL on

The display driver programs the HDMI PLL registers directly. As an
unused clock, the PLL was turned off at boot and the display froze.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/clk/meson/t7-pll.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/meson/t7-pll.c b/drivers/clk/meson/t7-pll.c
index 0a622f45f..736029cbf 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/meson/t7-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/meson/t7-pll.c
@@ -671,6 +671,11 @@ static struct clk_regmap t7_hdmi_pll_dco = {
 			{ .fw_name = "in0", }
 		},
 		.num_parents = 1,
+		/*
+		 * The display driver programs the HDMI PLL registers
+		 * directly: do not disable it as unused.
+		 */
+		.flags = CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED,
 	},
 };
 
